---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LEGAL, SITE } from '../site';
const L = LEGAL;
const fp = SITE.formEndpoint && SITE.formProvider.name ? SITE.formProvider : null;
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy" heading="Privacy policy · Datenschutzerklärung" updated={L.updated}>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
  <address>
    {L.name || '[Name]'}{L.trading && <>, {L.trading}</>}<br />
    {L.street || '[Street]'}, {L.city || '[Postcode City]'}, {L.country}<br />
    {L.email ? <a href={`mailto:${L.email}`}>{L.email}</a> : '[Email]'}
  </address>

  <h2>2. In short</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics, tracking, advertising or social-media
    plugins. Fonts and all other files are served from this site itself; your browser makes no
    requests to third parties while you read it — unless you choose to play an embedded video
    (section 5). Personal data is processed only as described below.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
    San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser necessarily transmits
    technical data to GitHub’s servers: IP address, date and time of the request, the page
    requested, the referring page, and browser and operating-system information. GitHub uses
    this data to deliver the site and to keep it secure, and may store it in server logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Obelisk installers are also served by GitHub, from GitHub Releases. When you click a
    download, your browser requests the file from GitHub’s servers and transmits the same
    technical data.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — our legitimate interest in a reliable and secure
    presentation of this website. Data may be transferred to the USA; GitHub, Inc. is certified
    under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, and the transfer relies on the European Commission’s
    adequacy decision for it (Art. 45 GDPR). Details:
    {' '}<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="early-access">4. Contacting us and early-access requests</h2>
  {fp ? (
    <>
      <p>
        If you use the early-access form, the details you enter — your email address and, if
        you provide them, your organisation, how you scan and your setup — are sent to our form
        service, {fp.name}, which receives the submission and forwards it to us by email. We use
        these details only to contact you about Obelisk.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), given with the checkbox on the form.
        The provider processes the data in the USA. There is no adequacy decision of the European
        Commission covering this provider, and US authorities may be able to access the data
        without the remedies available in the EU. By ticking the checkbox you explicitly consent to
        this transfer (Art. 49(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect
        for the future by emailing us; we then delete your details and ask the provider to delete
        the submission. See the provider’s <a href={fp.privacyUrl} rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </>
  ) : (
    <p>
      The early-access form does not send anything to a server. It opens your own email program
      with a pre-filled message addressed to us; nothing is transmitted until you send that email
      yourself.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>
    When you email us, we process your email address and whatever you include in the message in
    order to reply and to handle your request — for early-access requests, to contact you about
    Obelisk. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your message concerns a possible
    contract, and otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our interest in answering enquiries). We delete
    the correspondence once it is no longer needed, unless statutory retention periods apply.
    You can ask us to remove you from the early-access list at any time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="video">5. Embedded video (YouTube)</h2>
  <p>
    Where a page contains a video, it shows a still image from this site in its place, and your
    browser makes no connection to YouTube. The YouTube player is loaded only when you click
    that image. It is then loaded in YouTube’s privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com), a
    service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once you click, your browser connects to Google’s servers and transmits at least your IP
    address, browser and device information and the address of the page you are on. YouTube
    may store information on your device (cookies or similar technologies) and may use the
    data for its own purposes. Data may be transferred to the USA; Google LLC is certified
    under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, and the transfer relies on the European
    Commission’s adequacy decision for it (Art. 45 GDPR).
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, and § 25(1) TDDDG for storing or
    reading information on your device), which you give by clicking the video after the notice
    beside it. It applies to that page view only; if you prefer, you can watch the video on
    youtube.com instead or not at all. Details:
    {' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR);</li>
    <li>have it corrected (Art. 16) or erased (Art. 17);</li>
    <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18) and receive it in a portable format (Art. 20);</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21);</li>
    <li>withdraw any consent you gave, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, email us at the address above. You also have the right to lodge a
    complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), in particular in the
    EU member state of your residence, your place of work or the place of the alleged infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this policy when the website or the way we process data changes — for
    example when Obelisk goes on sale. The current version is always on this page.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
